# The whole data/ directory (including data/raw/) ships in the image.
# A prior pass tried to exclude the raw/ subdirectories that only *seemed*
# to be scraping/processing-time input, reasoning from a partial code
# read -- that broke the regular Ironman races at runtime
# (parsers/ironman/regular_events.py parses data/raw/ironman_regular/ raw
# JSON directly on every load, no processed-CSV step exists for that one
# source, unlike every other source in this app). Given that mistake,
# shipping the ~190MB in full is worth more than the size savings.

.git/
.github/
.claude/
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
local/
tests/
scrape_and_process.ipynb
launch.bat
